IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc20-part16-reverse-onus`

-- ccc20-part16-principles.l4 -- sections 493.1, 493.11 and 493.2 of the Criminal Code (Canada): the principle of restraint and the attention owed to Aboriginal accused and to vulnerable populations. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text; nothing is claimed verified against the official text.
-- An answer is JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A duty and a bar answer JUST FALSE when their gate fails; a rule whose scope is a named complement (a peace officer, a justice or a judge)
-- answers NOTHING for any other person (a scope limit with no "only": ruling (c)). The decision-maker is the core's `Party` (`a peace officer`, `a justice`, `a judge`).
-- This module is last in the order of writing because section 493.11(2)(c) and (e) call answers of later sections: s 515(6), s 522(2), s 523(2.1), s 524(4) and s 515(10) are asked as MAYBE BOOLEAN inputs and carried through.
-- The conditions of the other modules (ss 498(1.1), 501(3), 515(6), 515(10), 522(2), 523(2.1), 524(4)) answer their own questions; the principles here say how a decision-maker is to weigh them.

§ `Section 493.1 -- Principle of restraint`

-- 493.1 "In making a decision under this Part, a peace officer, justice or judge shall give primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity and on the least onerous
-- conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances, including conditions that are reasonably practicable for the accused to comply with, while taking into account the grounds referred to in subsection 498(1.1)
-- or 515(10), as the case may be." For the purposes of section 493.1, section 493.11(2)(c) says that a justice or judge shall NOT give that primary consideration to an accused to whom 515(6), 522(2), 523(2.1) or
-- 524(4) applies; the function below therefore takes the answer of section 493.11(2)(c) (fork F-493.1-with-493.11-2-c).
-- src:11059 | 493.1 In making a decision under this Part, a peace officer, justice or judge shall give primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity and on the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances, including conditions that are reasonably practicable for the accused to comply with, while taking into account the grounds referred to in subsection 498(1.1) or 515(10), as the case may be.
@ref s 493.1 (src:11059)
GIVEN maker IS A Party
      `the decision is made under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 493.11(2)(c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 493.1 the peace officer, justice or judge must give primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity and on the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the decision is made under this Part` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In making a decision under this Part, a peace officer, justice or judge shall give primary consideration"
        IF NOT (maker EQUALS `a peace officer` OR maker EQUALS `a justice` OR maker EQUALS `a judge`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a peace officer, justice or judge shall give primary consideration" (the duty is for the three named)
        IF (maker EQUALS `a justice` OR maker EQUALS `a judge`) AND `the answer of s 493.11(2)(c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) a justice or judge, as the case may be, shall not give primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity if the accused is one to whom subsection 515(6), 522(2), 523(2.1) or 524(4) applies" (section 493.11(2) applies "for the purposes of section 493.1")
        IF (maker EQUALS `a justice` OR maker EQUALS `a judge`) AND `the answer of s 493.11(2)(c)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 493.11(2)(c) rests on an answer of a section outside this range (s 469, s 3.01) that is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 493.1 the grounds (src:11059)
GIVEN `the decision is made under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 493.1 the decision-maker must take into account the grounds referred to in subsection 498(1.1) or 515(10), as the case may be` MEANS
    IF `the decision is made under this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In making a decision under this Part, a peace officer, justice or judge shall give primary consideration ... while taking into account the grounds referred to in subsection 498(1.1) or 515(10), as the case may be"

§ `Section 493.11 -- Clarification and application of the principle of restraint`

-- 493.11 (1) "For greater certainty, section 493.1 does not require the accused to be released."
-- src:11061 | 493.11 (1) For greater certainty, section 493.1 does not require the accused to be released.
@ref s 493.11(1) (src:11061)
`s 493.11(1) section 493.1 requires the accused to be released` MEANS
    JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "section 493.1 does not require the accused to be released"

-- 493.11 (2) "For the purposes of section 493.1, (a) a peace officer shall not release the accused if the peace officer believes on reasonable grounds that it is necessary in the public interest for the accused
-- to be detained in custody under subsection 498(1.1), including for the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence; ..."
-- src:11063 | (2) For the purposes of section 493.1,
-- src:11064 | (a) a peace officer shall not release the accused if the peace officer believes on reasonable grounds that it is necessary in the public interest for the accused to be detained in custody under subsection 498(1.1), including for the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence;
@ref s 493.11(2)(a) (src:11063-11064)
GIVEN maker IS A Party
      `the peace officer believes on reasonable grounds that it is necessary in the public interest for the accused to be detained in custody under subsection 498(1.1), including for the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 493.11(2)(a) the peace officer is barred from releasing the accused` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT maker EQUALS `a peace officer` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) a peace officer shall not release the accused"
        IF `the peace officer believes on reasonable grounds that it is necessary in the public interest for the accused to be detained in custody under subsection 498(1.1), including for the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a peace officer shall not release the accused if the peace officer believes on reasonable grounds that it is necessary in the public interest for the accused to be detained in custody under subsection 498(1.1)" (a bar whose "if" gate fails is not engaged)

-- "(b) a peace officer shall, if they release the accused, impose the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances, namely, those that are necessary to address the risks posed by the accused
-- as they relate to the purposes referred to in subsection 501(3), including the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence;"
-- src:11065 | (b) a peace officer shall, if they release the accused, impose the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances, namely, those that are necessary to address the risks posed by the accused as they relate to the purposes referred to in subsection 501(3), including the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence;
@ref s 493.11(2)(b) (src:11065)
GIVEN maker IS A Party
      `the peace officer releases the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 493.11(2)(b) the peace officer must impose the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT maker EQUALS `a peace officer` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) a peace officer shall, if they release the accused, impose the least onerous conditions"
        IF `the peace officer releases the accused` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a peace officer shall, if they release the accused, impose the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances"

@ref s 493.11(2)(b) namely (src:11065)
GIVEN `the condition is necessary to address the risks posed by the accused as they relate to the purposes referred to in subsection 501(3), including the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 493.11(2)(b) the condition is one of the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` MEANS
    IF `the condition is necessary to address the risks posed by the accused as they relate to the purposes referred to in subsection 501(3), including the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances, namely, those that are necessary to address the risks posed by the accused as they relate to the purposes referred to in subsection 501(3)"

-- "(c) a justice or judge, as the case may be, shall not give primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity if the accused is one to whom subsection 515(6), 522(2),
-- 523(2.1) or 524(4) applies;" The four answers come from the later modules: one MAYBE BOOLEAN each, "any answer holds" over them.
-- src:11066 | (c) a justice or judge, as the case may be, shall not give primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity if the accused is one to whom subsection 515(6), 522(2), 523(2.1) or 524(4) applies;
@ref s 493.11(2)(c) (src:11066)
GIVEN maker IS A Party
      `the answers of s 515(6), s 522(2), s 523(2.1) and s 524(4) for the accused` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 493.11(2)(c) the justice or judge is barred from giving primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (maker EQUALS `a justice` OR maker EQUALS `a judge`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(c) a justice or judge, as the case may be, shall not give primary consideration"
        IF `s 515(6) helper: any answer holds` `the answers of s 515(6), s 522(2), s 523(2.1) and s 524(4) for the accused` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 515(6) helper: any answer holds` `the answers of s 515(6), s 522(2), s 523(2.1) and s 524(4) for the accused` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): one of the four answers rests on a section outside this range (s 469, s 3.01) and is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not give primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity if the accused is one to whom subsection 515(6), 522(2), 523(2.1) or 524(4) applies" (none of the four applies: a bar whose "if" gate fails is not engaged)

-- "(d) a justice or judge shall, if they release the accused, impose the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances, namely, those that are necessary to address the risks posed by the
-- accused as they relate to the grounds referred to in subsection 515(10), including the protection or safety of the public; and"
-- src:11067 | (d) a justice or judge shall, if they release the accused, impose the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances, namely, those that are necessary to address the risks posed by the accused as they relate to the grounds referred to in subsection 515(10), including the protection or safety of the public; and
@ref s 493.11(2)(d) (src:11067)
GIVEN maker IS A Party
      `the justice or judge releases the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 493.11(2)(d) the justice or judge must impose the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (maker EQUALS `a justice` OR maker EQUALS `a judge`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(d) a justice or judge shall, if they release the accused, impose the least onerous conditions"
        IF `the justice or judge releases the accused` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a justice or judge shall, if they release the accused, impose the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances"

@ref s 493.11(2)(d) namely (src:11067)
GIVEN `the condition is necessary to address the risks posed by the accused as they relate to the grounds referred to in subsection 515(10), including the protection or safety of the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 493.11(2)(d) the condition is one of the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` MEANS
    IF `the condition is necessary to address the risks posed by the accused as they relate to the grounds referred to in subsection 515(10), including the protection or safety of the public`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances, namely, those that are necessary to address the risks posed by the accused as they relate to the grounds referred to in subsection 515(10)"

-- "(e) a justice or judge shall not order that the accused be released if the detention of the accused is justified under subsection 515(10), including for the protection or safety of the public."
-- src:11068 | (e) a justice or judge shall not order that the accused be released if the detention of the accused is justified under subsection 515(10), including for the protection or safety of the public.
@ref s 493.11(2)(e) (src:11068)
GIVEN maker IS A Party
      `the answer of s 515(10): the detention of the accused is justified` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 493.11(2)(e) the justice or judge is barred from ordering that the accused be released` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (maker EQUALS `a justice` OR maker EQUALS `a judge`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(e) a justice or judge shall not order that the accused be released"
        IF `the answer of s 515(10): the detention of the accused is justified` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the answer of s 515(10): the detention of the accused is justified` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of s 515(10) is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not order that the accused be released if the detention of the accused is justified under subsection 515(10)" (a bar whose "if" gate fails is not engaged)

§ `Section 493.2 -- Aboriginal accused and vulnerable populations`

-- 493.2 "In making a decision under this Part, a peace officer, justice or judge shall give particular attention to the circumstances of (a) Aboriginal accused; and (b) accused who belong to a vulnerable
-- population that is overrepresented in the criminal justice system and that is disadvantaged in obtaining release under this Part." "Aboriginal" and "vulnerable population" are not defined in this Part: plain inputs.
-- src:11070 | 493.2 In making a decision under this Part, a peace officer, justice or judge shall give particular attention to the circumstances of
-- src:11071 | (a) Aboriginal accused; and
-- src:11072 | (b) accused who belong to a vulnerable population that is overrepresented in the criminal justice system and that is disadvantaged in obtaining release under this Part.
@ref s 493.2 (src:11070-11072)
GIVEN `the accused is an Aboriginal accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 493.2(a) the accused is an Aboriginal accused, to whose circumstances particular attention must be given` MEANS
    IF `the accused is an Aboriginal accused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) Aboriginal accused" (paragraph (a) names Aboriginal accused; for an accused who is not one, only paragraph (b) can apply)

@ref s 493.2(b) (src:11072)
GIVEN `the accused belongs to a vulnerable population that is overrepresented in the criminal justice system and that is disadvantaged in obtaining release under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 493.2(b) the accused belongs to a vulnerable population, to whose circumstances particular attention must be given` MEANS
    IF `the accused belongs to a vulnerable population that is overrepresented in the criminal justice system and that is disadvantaged in obtaining release under this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) accused who belong to a vulnerable population that is overrepresented in the criminal justice system and that is disadvantaged in obtaining release under this Part" (paragraph (b) names accused who belong to such a population; for an accused who does not, only paragraph (a) can apply)

@ref s 493.2 (src:11070-11072)
GIVEN maker IS A Party
      `the decision is made under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of paragraph (a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of paragraph (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 493.2 the peace officer, justice or judge must give particular attention to the circumstances of the accused` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the decision is made under this Part` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In making a decision under this Part, a peace officer, justice or judge shall give particular attention"
        IF NOT (maker EQUALS `a peace officer` OR maker EQUALS `a justice` OR maker EQUALS `a judge`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a peace officer, justice or judge shall give particular attention" (the duty is for the three named)
        IF `the answer of paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer of paragraph (b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the circumstances of (a) Aboriginal accused; and (b) accused who belong to a vulnerable population" (the text does not say "only": an accused in neither is not covered)
